    "title": "Fire weather watch issued for Alabama for Saturday",
    "text": "WeatherPublished: Mar. 26, 2026, 5:20 p.m.Low humidity and gusty winds could raise the fire danger on Saturday. Above are the forecast wind gusts for Saturday.National Weather ServiceThe National Weather Service is raising concerns about the potential for wildfires on Saturday in Alabama. The weather service has issued a fire weather watch for all of north and central Alabama for Saturday. The watch will be in effect from 7 a.m. until 7 p.m.The weather service said a dry cold front will move through Alabama starting on Friday night. Behind the front forecasters expect humidity levels to drop and winds to pick up, which will make it easier for fires to start and spread.The weather service is forecasting humidity levels to be as low as 19 to 23 percent on Saturday. Winds could gust up to 30 mph.The weather service said that “any fires that develop will likely spread rapidly. Please obey any local burn bans that are in place!\"A fire weather watch is a precursor to what’s called a “red flag warning.”RECOMMENDEDA red flag warning is issued when “critical” fire conditions are expected to occur or are occurring within the next 24 hours.Some tips from the weather service:Avoid open flames or sparksKeep vehicles off dry grassProperly discard cigarettesLeigh Morgan is an Alabama native. She has written about weather for AL.com since 2013 and has been a weather nerd since Hurricane Frederic slammed into the Alabama coast in 1979. She started out in journalism...",
